## Voxels, 1: a chunk is an array. 16 by 16 by 16 block numbers built
## from a height field in a few array expressions -- grass, dirt, stone,
## water below a level, sand at its shore, one tree -- then counted,
## cut and seen from above. (docs/voxels.md; the next demos draw it.)
## Run: just demo scene voxels-chunk   (pictures go to work/draw/)

"vx:" u_se< "Voxels"

h := vx:h_ills 0.0
"the height field (x across, z down), 3 to 12:"
h
b := vx:c_hunk h
s_hape b
"blocks of each kind:"
vx:names
vx:c_ounts b

"the slice at x = 8, looking east (up is up):"
8 vx:s_ide b
"the slice at x = 4, through the tree:"
4 vx:s_ide b

"seen from above (the top block of each column):"
t := vx:t_op b
t
p := []S_HOW []G_RID t
p := []S_HOW []G_RID r_ev (1 + 8 s_elect b)
"drawn: the view from above, the slice at x = 8"
